flight:
The ample treasure of her secret stores;
Swift from above the wings her silent flight
Through Phoebe's realms, fair regent of the night;

flint:
Therefore in patience I possess my soul;
Yea, therefore as a flint I set my face,
To pluck down, to build up again the whole--

flirting:
Wild May that cantered by the risky ways,
With showy head-cloth flirting in the wind,
From market in the glad December days;

flicker:
I will not quiver in the frailest bone,
You will not note a flicker of defeat;
My heart shall tremble not its fate to meet,

flits:
In amber lies;
Approached, the amber flits a little, --
And that 's the skies!

flings:
I flung closer to his breast,
As sword that, after battle, flings to sheathe;
And, in that hurtle of united souls,

flip:
Insufficient that I match you
Every coin you flip;
Your demand is that I catch you

flippant:
A purple finger on the slope;
A flippant fly upon the pane;
A spider at his trade again;

flirted:
